module

public import Theory.Mathieu.M24.ValueBoundParabolics
public import Theory.Mathieu.M24.ValueBoundParabolics.Construction.Cosets
public import Theory.Mathieu.M24.ValueBoundParabolics.Construction.Generation

/-!
# A native generating triple of minimal M₂₄ Sylow overgroups

The three subgroups are generated by the marked Sylow generators and three
explicit additional Witt-design permutations. Checked three-coset tables give
order 3072 for each. Short prime-order words and the simple-group coset action
prove that they generate M₂₄. The existing value-bound interface supplies
properness and the intrinsic S₃ quotients from this order and containment.

This is the native-group construction used in Aschbacher–Smith, E.4.3(2),
printed pp.241–242 (PDF pp.252–253). Transport to the source's ambient group
and the representation bound are separate consumers of this theorem.
-/

public section
namespace Sporadic.Mathieu.M24ValueBoundParabolics

/-- Three actual order-3072 overgroups of the marked Sylow subgroup generate M₂₄. -/
theorem exists_native_triple : ∃ P : Fin 3 → Subgroup M24,
    (∀ i, M24LocalGeometry.SylowNormalizer.candidate ≤ P i) ∧
    (∀ i, Nat.card (P i) = 3072) ∧ (⨆ i, P i) = ⊤ :=
  ⟨Construction.parabolic, Construction.candidate_le_parabolic,
    Construction.parabolic_card, Construction.parabolic_iSup⟩

end Sporadic.Mathieu.M24ValueBoundParabolics
